  "description": "UQEDED crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C118 H136 Cl2 Co6 Gd4 N14 O36,3(C2 H3 N1),9(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.182-3.895 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.13-113.31°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co6Gd4(HL)4(pdmH)2(pdm)8Cl2]·3CH3CN·9H2O (C118H154Cl2Co6Gd4N14O45; Mr = 3542.06; CCDC formula C118H136Cl2Co6Gd4N14O36·3(C2H3N)·9(H2O)). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
